patrone-file-manager (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Tabs keep a fixed width. Dragging a window's only tab moves the window;
    a tab pulled out of the strip (or dragged with Ctrl) joins another
    window's tabs when dropped on its title bar, or opens in a window of its
    own. "Move to new window" moves the tab itself; "Move to window" lists
    the other windows. Files dropped on a tab go into its folder.
  * A tab's close button works again: the tab no longer takes the click.
  * Commands typed in the address bar run in the folder on screen, as in
    Windows: apps with windows directly, anything else in a terminal that
    stays open; Windows' names (cmd, notepad, explorer...) work; cd PLACE
    goes there.
  * System folder hints (View > Show, Folder Options > View): tags saying
    what system folders and well-known files are for, a banner with the
    Windows equivalent, and the matching commands in Permissions.
  * Permissions: changeable owner and group, "Allow running this file as a
    program", the special permissions, applying to everything inside a
    folder, the mode as numbers and letters, and changes as administrator
    through pkexec when they need it.
  * System folders have their own icons; the special folders' emblems and
    the system drive's mark are larger.
  * Text in Patrone's typeface (Inter) at Windows' 9 points, with larger
    icons in the lists; the empty-folder message sits in the middle.

